{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791592383,"nonce":"qEesk3zsMjve3Lg2cAKU6AXsLBA=","title":"Python inference re-infers items whose inputs did not change","message":"infer_module infers every item in each inner round until nothing changes, then once more for the dynamic-methods pass, and the outer loop in parse_program_once calls it until the globals, list facts, dynamic methods and field lists settle (go: 5 calls of 4 inner rounds over 51 items). Inference is about a third of go's start-up (infer_module 3890 of 11599 samples, ZYPY_PROFILE_STARTUP=300, Apple M-series).\n\nA probe fingerprinted each item's inference result (locals, list facts, passed argument types, field rounds) and the module state it ran against (signatures, class fields, closures, list params, field lists, dynamic fields, per-class fields, globals, dynamic methods, dict/set shape classes):\n\n  kernel     inferences  same result as the item's previous one in the call  same as any earlier one  state unchanged since previous\n  go         1133        664 (59%)                                           996 (88%)                164 (14%)\n  richards   1071        685 (64%)                                           944 (88%)                124\n  raytrace   1146        634 (55%)                                           1006 (88%)               27\n  nbody       297        153 (52%)                                           253 (85%)                5\n  fft         804        498 (62%)                                           721 (90%)                112\n  deltablue  1245        787 (63%)                                           1077 (87%)               168\n\nIn all six, the call that restarts after a class gained fields (the \"grew\" path) reproduced the previous call's per-item results exactly.\n\nA version of the whole module state skips little (last column). Recording what each item's inference reads (which signatures, which classes' fields, which closures, list facts, field lists, dynamic fields, per-class fields, shape classes) and re-inferring an item only when one of those changed would skip most of the inner rounds; reusing results across calls needs the item's effects replayed into the fresh module as well.","files":null}]}